s-even-the-oddly-specific-ones/283831","site":"T Nation · 1913 posts · 2023"},{"title":"Ever Feel Like A Threadkiller? 41","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/ever-feel-like-a-threadkiller-41/164812","site":"T Nation · 1295 posts · 2011"},{"title":"The Dating Thread","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-dating-thread/275759","site":"T Nation · 1209 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Outside of gym culture no one really cares","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/outside-of-gym-culture-no-one-really-cares/294042","site":"T Nation · 953 posts · 2026"},{"title":"Calisthenics for 6 Months, Progress Slower Than What is Normal","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/calisthenics-for-6-months-progress-slower-than-what-is-normal/259465","site":"T Nation · 873 posts · 2019"},{"title":"Radical positions","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/radical-positions/288879","site":"T Nation · 548 posts · 2024"},{"title":"Does Anyone Else Here Collect Guns?","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/does-anyone-else-here-collect-guns/277616","site":"T Nation · 462 posts · 2022"},{"title":"MIT Eliminates DEI Hiring Requirements","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/mit-eliminates-dei-hiring-requirements/287489","site":"T Nation · 439 posts · 2024"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Nutrient timing - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutrient_timing"},{"title":"Bodybuilding - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodybuilding"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Muscle","chain":["Carbs around workouts","Restored muscle glycogen","Better training and recovery, more muscle"],"effect":"indirect","text":"Lifters schedule carbs such as sweet potato around training to fuel sessions and speed recovery, in pursuit of more muscle. Carbs refill muscle glycogen, which supports harder training and recovery. Glycogen replacement after exercise is studied, while the benefit of exact timing for physique is debated."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Carbohydrate timing refers to the idea that when carbohydrates are eaten around training affects performance and recovery. Wikipedia describes nutrient timing as coordinating intake with exercise, with claims that carbohydrates during and after workouts help replace muscle glycogen.[1]","A suggested post-exercise \"anabolic window\" of about 15 to 45 minutes is described as a suggestion rather than an established fact, and the article says timing is not essential to good performance.[1] Sweet potato as a particular carbohydrate source was not covered by the sources reviewed."],"infobox":[["Practice","Scheduling carbohydrate intake around training"],["Concept","Nutrient timing / anabolic window"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Proponents say that carbohydrate plus protein around workouts raises glycogen and protein synthesis after training.[1] Bodybuilding sources note that many lifters favour slow-digesting, low-glycemic carbohydrates, with faster sugars around workouts.[2]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Research","paras":["Reviews on the topic exist, including a 2017 International Society of Sports Nutrition position stand and a 2013 paper questioning whether a post-exercise anabolic window exists.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found on sweet potato specifically for carbohydrate timing. Studies of nutrient timing in general exist and are listed in the nutrient timing literature.[1]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":null,"timeline":[{"year":"2004","event":"Ivy and Portman publish the book Nutrient Timing.[1]"}],"refs":[{"title":"Nutrient timing - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutrient_timing","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Bodybuilding - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bodybuilding","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"}],"studies":[{"title":"Nutrient timing - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nutrient_timing","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-1/264067","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 2)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-2/273731","site":"T Nation · 8490 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Things That Piss You Off","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/things-that-piss-you-off/163775","site":"T Nation · 7426 posts · 2011"},{"title":"The Tactical Life","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-tactical-life/232312","site":"T Nation · 5251 posts · 2017"},{"title":"The Return of Even More Movies You've Watched This Week III","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/the-return-of-even-more-movies-youve-watched-this-week-iii/210398","site":"T Nation · 4744 posts · 2015"},{"title":"Boilerman Wants It All","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/boilerman-wants-it-all/254882","site":"T Nation · 4422 posts · 2019"}]}